   "source": [
    "## 5. Pandas Data Cleaning\n",
    "\n",
    "Real data is never clean and this dataset isn't either \u2014 there's missing values, some duplicate rows, gender typed differently in different places, and a couple of impossible values (negative age??). Checking all of that first before fixing anything."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "missing values:\n",
      " CustomerID              0\n",
      "Age                     0\n",
      "Gender                  0\n",
      "Region                  0\n",
      "Annual_Income          24\n",
      "Membership_Years        0\n",
      "Engagement_Score       24\n",
      "Avg_Session_Minutes    25\n",
      "Purchase_Frequency      0\n",
      "Discount_Usage_Rate     0\n",
      "Total_Spend             0\n",
      "Purchased               0\n",
      "dtype: int64\n",
      "\n",
      "duplicate rows: 15\n",
      "\n",
      "gender values found: <StringArray>\n",
      "['M', 'Female', 'Male', 'male', 'F']\n",
      "Length: 5, dtype: str\n",
      "\n",
      "negative age rows: 9\n",
      "negative income rows: 6\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print('missing values:\\n', df.isnull().sum())\n",
    "print('\\nduplicate rows:', df.duplicated().sum())\n",
    "print('\\ngender values found:', df['Gender'].unique())\n",
    "print('\\nnegative age rows:', (df['Age'] < 0).sum())\n",
    "print('negative income rows:', (df['Annual_Income'] < 0).sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Okay here's how I'm handling each issue and why:\n",
    "- **Duplicates** \u2014 just drop them, they're exact copies so no info lost.\n",
    "- **Gender labels** ('M', 'male', 'F' etc.) \u2014 standardize to Male/Female.\n",
    "- **Negative age** \u2014 this is obviously just a sign error (nobody is -45 years old), so take the absolute value instead of throwing the row away.\n",
    "- **Negative income** \u2014 unlike age this doesn't have an obvious fix, so treat it as missing instead of guessing a value.\n",
    "- **Missing numeric values** (income, engagement, session time) \u2014 fill with the median instead of the mean, since median isn't dragged around by outliers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "missing values left: 0\n",
      "duplicates left: 0\n",
      "gender values now: <StringArray>\n",
      "['Male', 'Female']\n",
      "Length: 2, dtype: str\n",
      "shape now: (800, 12)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df = df.drop_duplicates().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['Gender'] = df['Gender'].replace({'M': 'Male', 'F': 'Female', 'male': 'Male'})\n",
    "\n",
    "df['Age'] = df['Age'].abs()\n",
    "\n",
    "df.loc[df['Annual_Income'] < 0, 'Annual_Income'] = np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in ['Annual_Income', 'Engagement_Score', 'Avg_Session_Minutes']:\n",
    "    df[col] = df[col].fillna(df[col].median())\n",
    "\n",
    "print('missing values left:', df.isnull().sum().sum())\n",
    "print('duplicates left:', df.duplicated().sum())\n",
    "print('gender values now:', df['Gender'].unique())\n",
    "print('shape now:', df.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Data Transformation\n",
    "\n",
    "Adding a few extra columns that group customers into buckets \u2014 these are usually more useful for business people to look at than raw numbers."
